          "passage": "In a 2019 paper in *Science*, a research team led by Rosenberg and colleagues estimated population changes for North American breeding birds from 1970 to 2017. Working from continental-scale monitoring data, the team distinguished losses by biome and reported both the absolute number of birds lost and the percentage change relative to the 1970 baseline. A student summarizing the paper notes that biomes with the largest absolute losses are not always the ones with the largest proportional declines, and argues that this pattern is most clearly illustrated by comparing two biomes for which the absolute and percentage rankings disagree, namely _______",
