          "passage": "In her 1979 report on the Laetoli site in northern Tanzania, paleoanthropologist Mary Leakey described a 27-meter trail of fossilized footprints preserved in volcanic tuff and dating to roughly 3.6 million years ago. The depth and stride of the prints, she argued, ______ the conclusion that the hominin who made them had walked upright on two legs in a manner anatomically similar to modern humans, rather than only intermittently or with the swinging gait that knuckle-walking primates retain when they stand.",
