          "skill": "words-in-context",
          "passage": "Soil microbial ecologist Wei Cheng has spent much of his career studying the rhizosphere — the thin layer of soil immediately surrounding plant roots — and the chemical signals roots release into it. Although researchers have long recognized that microbial activity is unusually intense in this zone, they have struggled to predict how a particular plant's root exudates will ______ the rate at which surrounding soil organic matter is decomposed by microbes. In a 2009 review, Cheng argued that the answer depends on the prior nutrient status of the soil, on the chemical composition of the exudates themselves, and on which microbial groups happen to be locally abundant.",
